    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1066">

                <pb facs="0952" n="848" xml:id="pg848"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/9318.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to Belgium to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-10-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s October 14, 7 p.m. The Belgian Government, as a secondary and
                    neutral power, is prevented by traditional policy from comment thereon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marburg</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
